Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
Return-path: <linux-kernel-owner@vger.kernel.org>
In-Reply-To: <1502367012-9417-1-git-send-email-cakturk@gmail.com>
Sender: linux-kernel-owner@vger.kernel.org
Cc: daniel@ffwll.ch, linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org, dri-devel@lists.freedesktop.org, Cihangir Akturk <cakturk@gmail.com>, Alex Deucher <alexander.deucher@amd.com>, =?UTF-8?q?Christian=20K=C3=B6nig?= <christian.koenig@amd.com>, David Airlie <airlied@linux.ie>, Alex Xie <AlexBin.Xie@amd.com>, Mario Kleiner <mario.kleiner.de@gmail.com>, Michal Hocko <mhocko@kernel.org>, Matthew Wilcox <mawilcox@microsoft.com>, Monk Liu <Monk.Liu@amd.com>, Chunming Zhou <David1.Zhou@amd.com>, Dave Airlie <airlied@redhat.com>, Junwei Zhang <Jerry.Zhang@amd.com>, =?UTF-8?q?Marek=20Ol=C5=A1=C3=A1k?= <marek.olsak@amd.com>, Andres Rodriguez <andresx7@gmail.com>, =?UTF-8?q?Michel=20D=C3=A4nzer?= <michel.daenzer@amd.com>, Daniel Vetter <daniel.vetter@ffwll.ch>, Harry
List-Id: amd-gfx.lists.freedesktop.org

Use drm_*_get() and drm_*_put() helpers instead of drm_*_reference()
and drm_*_unreference() helpers.

drm_*_reference() and drm_*_unreference() functions are just
compatibility alias for drm_*_get() and drm_*_put() and should not be
used by new code. So convert all users of compatibility functions to
use the new APIs.

Generated by: scripts/coccinelle/api/drm-get-put.cocci

Signed-off-by: Cihangir Akturk <cakturk@gmail.com>
Reviewed-by: Christian König <christian.koenig@amd.com>
---
